Original commit body from 96eb435c1a60b7e8949ea97fd9edb6f3f2f059c8:

Completes the manifest-union fix. The MERGE path was corrected to select
entries by section rather than by path prefix; the REPORTING path three lines
away kept the old predicate:

    _mf_sliced=$(grep -c '^packages/' "$_mf_regen" ...)

A manifest of root-level `tests/...` entries -- the common shape, and the exact
shape of the 95-entry manifest that motivated the whole fix -- counts 0 under
that pattern. Both sides came out 0, the guard `final > sliced` was never true,
and the one line that makes a silent narrowing VISIBLE never printed.

A DIAGNOSTIC THAT CANNOT FIRE IS WORSE THAN NO DIAGNOSTIC, because its silence
is indistinguishable from "nothing needed preserving" -- which is precisely the
false all-clear the union exists to end.

This is ONE FACT IN TWO HOMES and the second silently won (LIVE.md rule 9),
committed on my own diff within one PR of fixing it the first time. The remedy
is structural rather than a second correction: section-reading now has exactly
ONE implementation, `_manifest_selected_tests`, and both the merge path and the
new `_manifest_test_count` call it. There is no second home left to drift.

Neither cut was caught by a failing test. The first was caught by checking the
pattern against the real manifest, the second by noticing the shield line did
not appear in a live auto-pr run where it should have. Both wrong answers were
a plausible ZERO rather than an error.

Verified on the real repository manifest: sliced=1 final=95 now prints
"kept 94 committed manifest entry/entries the slicer did not select", where it
previously printed nothing. 11 union tests pass (two new ones pin the count
against root-level and package-level paths); smart-test 1,624 passed, ratchet
clean.

Governance files (scripts/auto-pr, scripts/lib/forgejo-api.sh) -- covered by
the human approval given for the manifest-overwrite fix, including merging
without --gov.

